# Mystic Warrior

**Alignments.** Any, but most are good or selfish.

A very powerful psychic whose powers are physical and combat-oriented - a
master psionic the book ranks beside the Mind Melter, second only to the Fetish
Shaman in renown as a war chief. Psionic spears and tomahawks are the class''s
legend, along with pyrokinesis, hydrokinesis and telekinesis, a spoken word that
bends a foe''s mind and a gaze that brings agony or blindness.

Its powers are believed to come from the ancestor spirits and the gods, and are
awakened one Vision Quest at a time. Many adopt a tribe or town as its protector
and war chief; many wander in search of wrongs to right, some of them chosen
agents of the gods guided by dreams and omens.

## Fetishes

Mystic Warriors start with two minor fetishes of choice and the Great Armor
Fetish. A further minor fetish is typically awarded at levels 5 and 10, a second
major one at level 3 (typically the Great Body, Superhuman Strength or
Supernatural Damage Fetish), and another for great heroism no sooner than
level 6.

## Lore

About one Mystic Warrior in eight is a woman (printed 37). The class''s powers
are believed to be the gift of the ancestor spirits and the gods rather than the
warrior''s own, which is why each one must be awakened by the spirits, and its
psionic spears and tomahawks are the stuff of legend across the West.

## Equipment the catalog cannot hold yet

A traditional bow (or a modern compound or energy bow) with two dozen arrows and
six dipped in silver, a war club, tomahawk or spear, a hat or hooded cloak,
50 feet of rope, a ball of string, a week of dried meat and fruit, and war and
camouflage paint. A rifle and a revolver may suit some Traditionalists, never a
Pure One.
', 'published', 'data-script'
